/> It seems to me that it would be regarded as a personal form of advertising a particular product. I shouldn't think that would be a problem per se..But I'm not a lawyer so...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T14:39:39-08:00","id":68652,"title":"","content":"I've got a Hunter the Vigil symbol tattooed on my back, and a Hunter the Reckoning symbol tattooed on my left calf. It makes it easier for vampires to identify me, but so far, I'm still alive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T02:02:26-08:00","id":68907,"title":"","content":"Indeed. Plenty of people have them, and some of them look fantastic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T03:11:30-08:00","id":68933,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:RobotoRegular, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Some tattoos could infringe on copyrights. Generally speaking, the copyright holder must prove the copied work has a negative effect on the work's value or potential market. A tattoo artist who inks a cartoon character onto a client without obtaining permission from the original illustrator may be infringing by affecting the potential market of the character; the illustrator could sell drawings to tattoo parlours for use on clients. On the other hand, the client is less likely to be considered infringing, since his display of the work is usually not for profit and in most cases would not affect the work's value or market.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T06:56:47-08:00","id":69039,"title":"","content":"If you get a tattoo watch out for the Copyright Ninjas. They might attack you in your sleep and flay it off your body. Don't say I didn't warn you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T07:23:34-08:00","id":69054,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this is one cases where if they decided to pursue it, the public backlash could be so negative as to vastly outweigh the potential positives of protecting a copyright.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T09:10:14-08:00","id":69118,"title":"","content":"It's worth nothing that the person with the liability in a lawsuit stemming from the tattoo of a copyrighted work would be the tattoo artist, not the customer. Theoretically the courts could order the tattoo altered/removed, but CCP (as the IP owners, they'd have to be the ones that sue you) wouldn't be able to sue a person with a WOD image tattooed on their body directly.<br /> <br /> Tattoos are one of the very nebulous parts of modern copyright law. There isn't a lot of case law about them, and most lawsuits dealing with tattoos are when original art by the tattoo artist is being replicated without their permission (ex: the artist that did Mike Tyson's facial tattoo sued when the Hangover II had Ed Helm's character end up with a replica of Tyson's tattoo without the original artist's permission to do so).<br /> <br /> Even so there's a fairly large amount of practical reasons on top of social and moral reasons for most companies to not bother chasing down copyrighted images getting tattooed.<br /> <br /> First, as mentioned, they have to go after the tattoo artist, not the person with the tattoo. So there's a significant amount of legwork that can be involved just finding the right person to file the lawsuit against.<br /> <br /> Second, they'd have to beat back a derivative use defense. As tattooing is an art, the artist could claim that while the image looks the same, making it look the same on the contours of a human body combined with the person flair of the artist's own skills are sufficient derivation that it doesn't count as infringement. Essentially the argument would be that tattoos like this would fall under the same protections as pop art (like Warhol's Campbell's soup series).<br /> <br /> Third, even if the derivative use argument isn't accepted by the court, the tattoo artist could still claim it as fair use. In other words, it would fall into the category of copyright infringements we allow as a society as part of the balancing act of protecting the monetary value of copyrighted work to the creators so they can make a profit and the cultural value of the works to society at large. However, since fair use is inherently infringement, it isn't on CCP to prove the tattoo is not fair use (though it behooves them to make a strong case and not trust that the person they're suing can't make a good one), it is up to the tattoo artist to make the case that the tattoo is fair use. This is a big fat question mark though, since US law sets very little hard precedent here and judges individual cases by a set of criteria. Also, Jack, it is kinda really odd to copy something off a website in a thread about copyright infringements (<a href=\"http://smallbusiness.chron.com/tattoos-infringe-copyrights-48743.html#\" target=\"_blank\">http://smallbusiness.chron.com/tatto...ts-48743.html#</a>) without citations; esp. when it is kinda wrong and written by a person trained in the sciences, not an IP lawyer.<br /> <br /> There's also a rather large issue with whether or not transfer paper is used, or if the tattoo artist does the ink free hand. Theoretically, using transfer paper for original works strengthens a tattoo artists legal ability to sue anyone that uses their tattoos without permission, but would weaken their defense of a work they did that copied existing art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T10:36:09-08:00","id":69194,"title":"","content":"I'd also chime in that since OPP/White Wolf/CCP are all very friendly with such things, I doubt anyone is going to have a problem unless you having the tattoo in any way causes a negative reaction for the companies in question. Being a Neo-Nazi, media darling racist, or going crazy and shooting up a crowd while screaming that the world of darkness is real and they're vampires comes to mind. of course the last one would likely result in a general sort of clamp down if anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T11:35:58-08:00","id":69257,"title":"","content":"I have a NWoD tat and everybody was fine with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T11:43:05-08:00","id":69266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/68511-whould-it-be-legal-for-me-to-get-classic-world-of-darkness-symbols-tattooed?p=69257#post69257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a NWoD tat and everybody was fine with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not everybody, you didn't ask ME! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T12:10:24-08:00","id":69284,"title":"","content":"I don't know a tattoo artist who will do a Disney character for fear of being sued, but I've never heard anyone say he wouldn't do a White Wolf symbol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T12:20:05-08:00","id":69287,"title":"","content":"White Wolf = +cool factor","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T14:25:38-08:00","id":69423,"title":"","content":"I was being lazy. I actually do have a law degree and the quote I gave is more valid than your advice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/68511-whould-it-be-legal-for-me-to-get-classic-world-of-darkness-symbols-tattooed?p=69118#post69118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth nothing that the person with the liability in a lawsuit stemming from the tattoo of a copyrighted work would be the tattoo artist, not the customer. Theoretically the courts could order the tattoo altered/removed, but CCP (as the IP owners, they'd have to be the ones that sue you) wouldn't be able to sue a person with a WOD image tattooed on their body directly.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The courts would be hard pressed to order the removal of a tattoo (meaning disfigurement and scarring). That would constitute a &quot;cruel and unusual punishment&quot; (see English Bill of Rights, the Eighth Amendment to the United States Constitution, Article Five of the Declaration of Human Right, et al.). There is also the Visual Artists Rights Act of 1990 (VARA) that gives artists a number of rights, chief of this point is artistic integrity, prohibiting works of art from being mutilated regardless of physical ownership or copyright.<br /> <br /> This is exemplified in Carter v. Helmsley-Spear, Inc.<br /> <br /> &quot;A bench trial was subsequently held in June and July 1994, at the conclusion of which the trial court granted the artists the permanent injunction prohibiting defendants from distorting, mutilating, modifying, destroying and removing plaintiffs' artwork.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The right of integrity allows the author to prevent any deforming or mutilating changes to his work, even after title in the work has been transferred.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Article 6bis of the Berne Convention protects attribution and integrity, stating in relevant part: Independently of the author's economic rights, and even after the transfer of the said rights, the author shall have the right to claim authorship of the work and to object to any distortion, mutilation or other modification of, or other derogatory action in relation to, the said work, which would be prejudicial to his honor or reputation.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Because they are personal to the artist, moral rights exist independently of an artist's copyright in his or her work.&quot;<br /> <br /> link: <a href=\"http://cyber.law.harvard.edu/metaschool/fisher/integrity/Links/Cases/carter.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://cyber.law.harvard.edu/metasch...es/carter.html</a><br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/68511-whould-it-be-legal-for-me-to-get-classic-world-of-darkness-symbols-tattooed?p=69118#post69118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, they'd have to beat back a derivative use defense. As tattooing is an art, the artist could claim that while the image looks the same, making it look the same on the contours of a human body combined with the person flair of the artist's own skills are sufficient derivation that it doesn't count as infringement. Essentially the argument would be that tattoos like this would fall under the same protections as pop art (like Warhol's Campbell's soup series).</div> </div> </div> </div>A 'derivative use defense' does not exist.<br /> <br /> Subject to <a href=\"http://www.copyright.gov/title17/92chap1.html#107\" target=\"_blank\">sections 107 through 122</a>, the owner of copyright under this title has the <b>exclusive rights</b> to do and to authorize any of the following:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">(1) to reproduce the copyrighted work in copies or phonorecords;<br /> <b>(2) to prepare derivative works based upon the copyrighted work;</b><br /> (3) to distribute copies or phonorecords of the copyrighted work to the public by sale or other transfer of ownership, or by rental, lease, or lending;<br /> (4) in the case of literary, musical, dramatic, and choreographic works, pantomimes, and motion pictures and other audiovisual works, to perform the copyrighted work publicly;<br /> (5) in the case of literary, musical, dramatic, and choreographic works, pantomimes, and pictorial, graphic, or sculptural works, including the individual images of a motion picture or other audiovisual work, to display the copyrighted work publicly; and<br /> (6) in the case of sound recordings, to perform the copyrighted work publicly by means of a digital audio transmission.</div>If it is not authorised, it is automatically an unlawful derivative work.<br /> <br /> link: <a href=\"http://www.copyright.gov/title17/92chap1.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.copyright.gov/title17/92chap1.html</a><br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/68511-whould-it-be-legal-for-me-to-get-classic-world-of-darkness-symbols-tattooed?p=69118#post69118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third, even if the derivative use argument isn't accepted by the court, the tattoo artist could still claim it as fair use. In other words, it would fall into the category of copyright infringements we allow as a society as part of the balancing act of protecting the monetary value of copyrighted work to the creators so they can make a profit and the cultural value of the works to society at large. However, since fair use is inherently infringement, it isn't on CCP to prove the tattoo is not fair use (though it behooves them to make a strong case and not trust that the person they're suing can't make a good one), it is up to the tattoo artist to make the case that the tattoo is fair use. This is a big fat question mark though, since US law sets very little hard precedent here and judges individual cases by a set of criteria. Also, Jack, it is kinda really odd to copy something off a website in a thread about copyright infringements (<a href=\"http://smallbusiness.chron.com/tattoos-infringe-copyrights-48743.html#\" target=\"_blank\">http://smallbusiness.chron.com/tatto...ts-48743.html#</a>) without citations; esp. when it is kinda wrong and written by a person trained in the sciences, not an IP lawyer.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It's kinda right; so says a lawyer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","user":"Jack","date":". 02-10-2014, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T07:45:18-08:00","id":69840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/68511-whould-it-be-legal-for-me-to-get-classic-world-of-darkness-symbols-tattooed?p=69266#post69266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not everybody, you didn't ask ME! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I tried to call you, but your number was disconnected! And you wanted me to get the Nosferatu symbol when I wanted the Frankenstein symbol.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T11:13:51-08:00","id":69923,"title":"","content":"I was going to make a sex joke about a misrepresentation lawsuit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T15:33:21-08:00","id":70086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/68511-whould-it-be-legal-for-me-to-get-classic-world-of-darkness-symbols-tattooed?p=69840#post69840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tried to call you, but your number was disconnected! And you wanted me to get the Nosferatu symbol when I wanted the Frankenstein symbol.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I thought it would look better where you were gonna put it. Once you moved the location, <i>of course</i> the Frankenstein one made more sense.......but you still didn't ask me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T22:47:46-07:00","id":91410,"title":"","content":"A little late, but I thought I'd share.<br /> <br /> I know Rich Thomas is responsible for basically every symbol for most of the game lines, and I'll say that I can only speak on my interactions with him but in no way am I attempting to speak for him. He very recently did color work on the Seers of Chronos symbol as a commission for me, one which was specifically designed for a future tattoo. He seemed to like the idea quite a bit, and did an amazing job. Said symbol is my current avatar, if you'd like to have a look. Given that, I'm pretty sure there would be no issues for you in regards to your own tattoo. It wouldn't hurt to ask him directly, just to be sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I'm immortal, I've been right so far&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/301-bwchism","name":"bwchism","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar301_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T23:14:08-07:00","id":91426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/68511-whould-it-be-legal-for-me-to-get-classic-world-of-darkness-symbols-tattooed?p=69423#post69423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was being lazy. I actually do have a law degree and the quote I gave is more valid than your advice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay, pissing contest, everyone loves those. They're <i>always</i> helpful...<br /> <br /> OP: Not a lawyer, very basic training in the theory of law as part of my criminology degree aside. But I would think that it'd be tricky to sue someone in Denmark for using a symbol from a US-based country in a way that is clearly not harming the company, or making the Dane any income. So you're probably safe. Plus, as other people have pointed out, WW/OPP is pretty cool about that kind of thing, which helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T12:35:59-07:00","id":91790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bwchism</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/68511-whould-it-be-legal-for-me-to-get-classic-world-of-darkness-symbols-tattooed?p=91410#post91410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A little late, but I thought I'd share.<br /> <br /> I know Rich Thomas is responsible for basically every symbol for most of the game lines, and I'll say that I can only speak on my interactions with him but in no way am I attempting to speak for him. He very recently did color work on the Seers of Chronos symbol as a commission for me, one which was specifically designed for a future tattoo. He seemed to like the idea quite a bit, and did an amazing job. Said symbol is my current avatar, if you'd like to have a look. Given that, I'm pretty sure there would be no issues for you in regards to your own tattoo. It wouldn't hurt to ask him directly, just to be sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point of clarity on this, Rich/OPP licenses the rights to use the IP from CCP specifically for RPG products. The property themselves are under the ownership and control of CCP. <br /> <br /> There would however not be the same issue with Trinity/Scion related things since they are owned outright by Rich/OPP, so for that stuff Rich could give a yes/no on things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T15:52:47-07:00","id":91901,"title":"","content":"No idea what the actual legal dimensions of this are... but many, many people, including me, have World of Darkness tattoos, and no incarnation of White Wolf has ever taken action over it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T18:38:31-07:00","id":92014,"title":"","content":"Once the Trinity Continuum logo is finalized, I am definitely planning on getting it tattooed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T08:25:47-07:00","id":92289,"title":"","content":"I'm considering getting the Order of Hermes and Tremere logos tattooed on me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T11:21:22-07:00","id":93606,"title":"","content":"I'm looking forward to the new \u00c6on trinity releases. I'm very happy that I bought the original collectors edition prior to the whole MTV/Aeon Flux issue, and even happier that I didn't send it back for the sticker solution. <br /> <br /> I have to give it to WW/CCP/OPP, there are tons of symbols that make awesome tattoos. I'm slowly doing some coloring work on many of my favorites, primarily the Sorcerers' Crusade symbols. After M20th has finished depleting my funds, I plan on another tattoo or two myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I'm immortal, I've been right so far&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/301-bwchism","name":"bwchism","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar301_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T04:27:40-07:00","id":94843,"title":"","content":"I highly doubt that they'd have an issue with you getting a tattoo of any of their products. Hell a buddy of mine has the Prime symbol tattoo'd on his arm. Besides, what is the chances of someone who works for the company, seeing you with the tattoo and going all the way to their boss and getting a case made out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T06:42:01-07:00","id":94898,"title":"","content":"Though the issue seems to be settled, I can't say I'm a big fan of the &quot;it's only illegal if you get caught&quot; line of justification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T11:14:04-07:00","id":95080,"title":"","content":"That's not quite the issue here though. There is a safe, no guessing, method: ask the IP-holder. I have no idea how easy it would be to ask CCP, but it seems like contacting Rich about the stuff that Onyx Path owns outright would be simple enough. If you get a yes, then there is no legal issue what-so-ever. <br /> <br /> Outside of that though, this is less of a &quot;it is only illegal if you get caught,&quot; and more of a, &quot;you can't know if it will be ruled illegal or not unless you get caught.&quot; There isn't a huge stack of consistent case-law to guide anyone here.<br /> <br /> Imagine if speed limits weren't hard lines, but guidelines that the police and the general public can apply some judgement on. So driving 10 mph over the limit on a clear day, one a easy stretch of road, while nobody is around for miles isn't inherently illegal because there's really no risk of harm. But going 1 mph below the limit in a blizzard with 5 foot visibility and horrible traction on even the straightest of roads could be considered unsafe driving and ticket-worthy.<br /> <br /> On one hand, this system allows for motorists and the police to make cases more situational and not have fines levied over an arbitrary number. On the other hand, it means that should there be a dispute about the safety of the speed someone was traveling, it becomes very sticky on what was, or was not, legal. An officer could pull you over for doing +15 mph over the suggested but in court both sides would be arguing over whether or not that was really dangerous in the situation or not.<br /> <br /> That is, basically, where IP law tends to be. The latitude that allows for cases to be handled so that each one is examined in its unique context also creates a huge amount of uncertainty over the legality of any edge cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}